gm-method/rendering (extend a procedural-scatter render distance WITHOUT 4x-ing the instance budget, parity-safe across a shared client-render/server-collider placement): doubling the render radius is 4x the area, so add a DISTANCE DENSITY FALLOFF -- a per-item keep-probability that is 1.0 near the camera and smoothsteps down to a small floor (>0, never bare) at the render distance. CRITICAL parity rule when the SAME deterministic placement function is imported by both the client visual layer AND a server physics/collider layer: the falloff must live ONLY in the CLIENT STREAMING layer (where the camera/player distance is known), NEVER in the shared placement function -- keep that byte-identical so client visual == server collider. Make the keep/drop a DETERMINISTIC coin keyed off a STABLE per-item id (a morton/trunk id), not a random or per-frame value, so the far field is stable frame-to-frame (no shimmer) and re-densifies consistently on approach. And set the full-density NEAR radius BEYOND the server collider ring, so every collider item sits in the always-kept band -> the thing a player shoots always exists on both runtimes (no phantom hits). Witness live: read the instance total at FULL fill (it should stay near the old full-density count, NOT 4x) + the per-distance-band histogram (per-area density falls) + fps (no regression). Lock with a source-shape test: falloff present in the client file, ABSENT (no camera/distance term) in the shared placement file.